  "summary": "A Sandy Springs, Georgia police officer, Francis Michael Esposito, resigned in August during an internal affairs investigation that found he used his department Flock ALPR credentials to run license-plate searches benefiting Signal 8, a private public-safety software startup founded by a former Sandy Springs detective. The department classified his exit as a termination and notified Flock Safety of the misuse.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Esposito used his Sandy Springs Police credentials to conduct searches in the Flock network for the purpose of informing Signal 8 algorithms, according to a police internal affairs report obtained by Appen Media.",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "Esposito's Flock queries were not made for law enforcement purposes, but instead \"for the benefit of a private company for which he was employed,\" the investigation alleges.",
      "paragraph_idx": 15
    },
    {
      "quote": "Frank Esposito was recently terminated after he failed to cooperate during an internal affairs investigation into possible misconduct",
      "paragraph_idx": 18
    },
    {
      "quote": "Upon learning of the situation last month, Flock promptly addressed it directly with Signal 8",
      "paragraph_idx": 23
    }
  ],
